4. COMMERCIAL DEPLOYMENT & ROYALTY OBLIGATIONS

Any commercial use, enterprise integration, or deployment of nodes within a distributed network requires a separate, fully executed Commercial Licensing and Royalty Agreement with the Licensor.

* Licensing Fees: Licensee shall pay the required upfront deployment and node-issuance fees.
* Royalty Payments: Licensee shall remit periodic, percentage-based royalties derived from gross revenues, subscription models, or network operational utility utilizing the Software.
* Reporting: Detailed usage logs, telemetry metrics, and financial accounts shall be provided to the Licensor on a strict quarterly basis.

5. NETWORK TELEMETRY, DATA ACCESS & MONITORING

By connecting, configuring, or operating any node utilizing the Software, the Licensee explicitly consents to continuous network telemetry monitoring. The Licensor reserves the right to track operational metrics, node health, network topology, transaction patterns, and usage statistics to ensure compliance, prevent abuse, and optimize network integrity.

6. REMOTE REVOCATION & NODE TERMINATION

The Licensor retains the unilateral right to instantly revoke cryptographic certificates, blacklist public keys, or terminate network synchronization for any node suspected of breaching this Agreement, engaging in unauthorized distribution, or violating intellectual property rights. Revocation is final and non-negotiable.

7. AUDIT AND COMPLIANCE

The Licensor reserves the right, upon reasonable notice, to audit network telemetry, operational logs, and financial records to verify compliance with deployment terms and ensure accurate calculation and payment of royalties. Licensee shall provide full transparency and cooperation during any audit.

